(10, 'Clinical', 'Which condition can lower-lobe pneumonia mimic?', 'Appendicitis, because it causes abdominal pain.', 2),
(11, 'Clinical', 'What are the signs of lobar consolidation?', 'Dullness to percussion, bronchial breathing and increased vocal resonance.', 1),
(12, 'Classification', 'How is a child with fast breathing and/or chest indrawing but no danger sign classified and treated (WHO, IMCI)?', 'As pneumonia, treated with oral amoxicillin at home.', 2),
